<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Addedomarus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Addedomarus was a British king known from his coins, who ruled the Trinovantes in what is now Essex in the late 1st century BCE. He was among the first rulers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to put his name on gold coinage, and he may have been buried in the rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lexden-tumulus">Lexden Tumulus</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camulodunum">Camulodunum</a>. His successors included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubnovellaunus">Dubnovellaunus</a>, before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunobelinus">Cunobelinus</a> of the Catuvellauni took over the area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/addedomarus.jpg" alt="Addedomarus" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Stat%C3%A8re,_or,_fonds_celtique,_Grande_Bretagne,_Type_A%C4%90%C4%90EDOMARVS_-_btv1b11291809n_(1_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
